                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Should an FMCG brand focus on D2C or quick commerce first?</h3>
                                        <p>Depends on category — perishables + high-frequency consumables lean quick-commerce first. Premium + subscription categories can lead with D2C.</p>
                                        <h3>What is a healthy FMCG marketing-to-net-sales ratio?</h3>
                                        <p>12-22% for growth-stage brands. Below 10% typically means under-investing; above 30% means burning cash on unprofitable growth.</p>
                                        <h3>Is TV worth it for FMCG at ₹50 Cr ARR?</h3>
                                        <p>Selectively yes — for brand building + trade support. Pure ROI is hard to measure; MMM helps quantify.</p>
                                        <h3>How do I handle marketplace + D2C pricing conflicts?</h3>
                                        <p>Different SKU strategy per channel, MRP consistency, exclusive bundles on brand.com.</p>
